1. Predict, then check
   r.clone()       r: &String     -> alloc::string::String
   rr.clone()      rr: &&String   -> &alloc::string::String
   ss.to_owned()   ss: &&str      -> &str
   shared.clone()  shared: Rc     -> alloc::rc::Rc<alloc::string::String>
   m.clone()       m: &mut String -> alloc::string::String

2. The three that were not a String, fixed by dereferencing to the right rung
   (*rr).clone()        -> alloc::string::String
   (*ss).to_owned()     -> alloc::string::String
   (*shared).clone()    -> alloc::string::String

3. The same three with no search at all: name the type, and the argument is coerced
   <String as Clone>::clone(rr)       -> alloc::string::String
   <str as ToOwned>::to_owned(ss)     -> alloc::string::String
   <String as Clone>::clone(&shared)  -> alloc::string::String
